# Living Engineering Handbook and Public Journal

Status: DONE
Milestone: D1 Initial illustrated edition, then continuous feature maintenance
Dependencies: None; implemented source and prior research are reference inputs, not release gates

## Purpose

Deliver the requested book-depth documentation, original diagrams, actual synthetic UI images and
public development journey, with an enforceable source-freshness workflow for future changes.

## Tasks

- [x] Study the owner's reference documentation read-only; adopt depth, not copied prose or assets.
- [x] Create the ordered22-chapter catalogue, first-principles onboarding and source-grounded chapters.
- [x] Author the public root JOURNAL with dated decisions, corrections, observations and limits.
- [x] Generate nine actual-WPF synthetic visual-tree images with source/image provenance.
- [x] Build a local Mermaid/Markdown/installed-browser pipeline; no hosted rendering or browser download.
- [x] Add maintenance rules to repository, feature/release workflows and definition of done.
- [x] Render and review all diagrams, offline HTML and printable PDF; fix actual content/layout issues.
- [x] Confirm full edition freshness, public links/citations and byte-identical script twins.
- [x] Record actual edition metrics and artifact receipt, preserving outstanding application qualification.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] All22chapters plus public journal are included, with implemented/planned/unknown labels.
- [x] Every chapter has source references, at least two diagrams and useful substantive exposition.
- [x] Every UI illustration is synthetic, labelled and linked to exact UI-source/image hashes.
- [x] HTML/PDF are locally generated and reviewed; the full edition passes freshness checks.
- [x] Later behavior/UI changes require corresponding docs/diagram/image/journal updates.
- [x] No real audio, chats, notes, credentials, desktop capture or cloud upload is used.
- [x] Azure Ask remains planned; Docker remains optional and last; no preview release is implied.

